    "help.section.faq.title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "help.faqSection.a36": "Open the campaign and select Report, choose a reason, and optionally add details. Your report is sent to ZRP's moderation team.",
    "help.faqSection.q36": "How do I report a ZRP Help campaign?",
    "help.faqSection.a35": "Contact ZRP Support to request organization verification.",
    "help.faqSection.q35": "How does an organization become verified to publish on ZRP Help?",
    "help.faqSection.a34": "Only verified organizations. This is enforced on ZRP's servers, so a standard account cannot publish a campaign.",
    "help.faqSection.q34": "Who can publish a ZRP Help campaign?",
    "help.faqSection.a33": "ZRP Help is a verified humanitarian space for people and communities affected by war, disaster, poverty, emergencies and other serious situations.",
    "help.faqSection.q33": "What is ZRP Help?",
    "help.faqSection.a32": "No, you can only submit one application per listing.",
    "help.faqSection.q32": "Can I apply to the same opportunity more than once?",
    "help.faqSection.a31": "It's a regular ZRP Opportunity listing - usually posted by the ZRP team - looking for someone to represent ZRP in a specific country. You apply to it the same way as any other listing.",
    "help.faqSection.q31": "What is a Country Manager opportunity?",
    "help.faqSection.a30": "My Applications shows every opportunity you've applied to. My Listings shows every opportunity you've posted, along with its review status and applicants.",
    "help.faqSection.q30": "Where can I see my applications and listings?",
    "help.faqSection.a29": "Open the listing and select Apply. You can add a cover note and attach a resume for listings that accept applications directly on ZRP; some listings link to an external application page instead.",
    "help.faqSection.q29": "How do I apply to an opportunity?",
    "help.faqSection.a28": "Any signed-in ZRP user. Every listing is reviewed by ZRP before it appears publicly.",
    "help.faqSection.q28": "Who can post an opportunity?",
    "help.faqSection.a27": "ZRP Opportunity is where the ZRP community posts and finds jobs, remote work, internships, scholarships, mentorships, freelance work, partnerships, sponsorships, hackathons, training and collaboration opportunities.",
    "help.faqSection.q27": "What is ZRP Opportunity?",
    "help.faqSection.a26": "ZRP Music doesn't currently have a dedicated report button on individual tracks. Contact ZRP Support with the track and artist details if you believe something violates your rights or ZRP's policies.",
    "help.faqSection.q26": "How do I report unauthorized or problematic music?",
    "help.faqSection.a25": "You're responsible for having the rights, license or permission for everything you upload - the audio, the artwork, and the accuracy of the artist and album information you provide.",
    "help.faqSection.q25": "What am I responsible for when I upload music?",
    "help.faqSection.a24": "Playing a track queues the rest of the list behind it, and you can add or remove individual tracks from the queue, clear it, and use shuffle or repeat.",
    "help.faqSection.q24": "How does the queue work?",
    "help.faqSection.a23": "Yes. Any signed-in listener can create playlists, add tracks to them, remove tracks, and play a playlist from Music.",
    "help.faqSection.q23": "Can I create playlists?",
    "help.faqSection.a22": "The tracks themselves are not deleted - they simply lose their album association and become standalone tracks again.",
    "help.faqSection.q22": "What happens to my tracks if I delete an album?",
    "help.faqSection.a21": "An album belongs to one artist and holds an ordered set of that artist's tracks. Create, edit and manage albums from Music Studio's Albums tab, including reordering or removing individual tracks.",
    "help.faqSection.q21": "How do albums work?",
    "help.faqSection.a20": "Yes. From Music Studio's Tracks tab you can edit a published track's details or delete it entirely.",
    "help.faqSection.q20": "Can I edit or delete a song after publishing it?",
    "help.faqSection.a19": "Open Music Studio, go to the Tracks tab, choose your audio file and cover artwork, add a title and genre, and publish.",
    "help.faqSection.q19": "How do I upload a song?",
    "help.faqSection.a18": "Music Studio is where an approved Creator or verified Artist uploads and manages their tracks and albums. It only appears once your account has publishing access.",
    "help.faqSection.q18": "What is Music Studio?",
    "help.faqSection.a17": "Accounts with Creator status (available on ZRP's Business or Enterprise plan) or a verified Music Artist profile. Creating an Artist Profile is open to anyone, but it must be verified by ZRP staff before you can publish.",
    "help.faqSection.q17": "Who can publish music on ZRP?",
    "help.faqSection.a16": "No. Listening to ZRP Music is open to ZRP users, but publishing music requires an approved Creator status or a verified Music Artist profile.",
    "help.faqSection.q16": "Can every ZRP user publish music?",
    "help.faqSection.a15": "Everyone. Listening, searching and discovering music on ZRP is open to all users; only publishing is restricted.",
    "help.faqSection.q15": "Who can listen to ZRP Music?",
    "help.faqSection.a14": "ZRP Music is ZRP Social's built-in music platform, where you can discover and play tracks, artists and albums, and - with the right status - publish your own music.",
    "help.faqSection.q14": "What is ZRP Music?",
    "help.aid.browseLink": "Open ZRP Help",
    "help.aid.reportIntro": "If a campaign looks suspicious or misleading, open it and select Report. Choose a reason and, optionally, add details - your report goes to ZRP's moderation team.",
    "help.aid.supportingIntro": "Signed-in users can contribute toward a campaign's goal, or offer non-monetary help such as supplies or volunteering, directly from a campaign's page.",
    "help.aid.supportingHeading": "Contributing & Offering Help",
    "help.aid.campaignC4": "Add supporting proof or documentation links",
    "help.aid.campaignC3": "Upload images to illustrate the situation",
    "help.aid.campaignC2": "Add a title, description, location and - for a money goal - the amount needed",
    "help.aid.campaignC1": "Choose a category and the type(s) of help needed",
    "help.aid.campaignHeading": "Creating a Campaign",
    "help.aid.verifiedHowText": "Contact ZRP Support to request organization verification. ZRP Help doesn't currently promise a fixed approval process or timeline.",
    "help.aid.verifiedHowTitle": "Becoming a Verified Organization",
    "help.aid.publishingIntro": "Only verified organizations can publish a ZRP Help campaign. This is checked on ZRP's servers, not just shown or hidden in the app, so a standard account can't publish a campaign even by working around the interface.",
    "help.aid.publishingHeading": "Who Can Publish a Campaign",
    "help.aid.categoriesIntro": "Every campaign is published under a category - War, Disaster, Poverty, Emergency or Other - so you can browse ZRP Help by the kind of situation you want to support.",
    "help.aid.intro": "ZRP Help is a verified humanitarian space for people and communities affected by war, disaster, poverty, emergencies and other serious humanitarian situations.",
